            <ArticleTitle>The Missing Ingredient In Quality Measurement.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14-15</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The measures most often used today to assess care quality are process measures. Actual outcomes, of course, are harder to measure than whether a certain action has been taken-checking the feet of a patient with diabetes, for example. But many experts don't think process measures get at the heart of quality.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
